# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
# Legacy single-file build output. `npm run build:single` regenerates it; it was
# purged from history on 2026-10-30 because a committed bundle bakes the
# publishable anon key into every commit.
production/
dist-ssr
*.local

# Environment files (contain Supabase project URLs and keys)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# .env.production is deliberately tracked: it carries only public build-time
# values (site URL + the publishable/anon key, which ships in the client bundle
# anyway) so a Vercel build can never silently ship without Supabase config.
!.env.production

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# Local agent workspace — tracked: content/seed/fix pipeline (seeders, content,
# mark schemes, golden-dump, SQL patches, PDF toolchain). Excluded: credential
# stores (get-keys.cjs), one-off verify/debug/test scripts, logs, thread-local docs.
.freebuff/*
!.freebuff/*.sql
!.freebuff/content-*.cjs
!.freebuff/seed-*.cjs
!.freebuff/notes-*.cjs
!.freebuff/mark-schemes-*.cjs
!.freebuff/apply-mark-schemes.cjs
!.freebuff/fix-quiz-answers.cjs
!.freebuff/fix-backticks*.cjs
!.freebuff/recover-backticks.cjs
!.freebuff/unescape-all.cjs
!.freebuff/unflatten-lessons.cjs
!.freebuff/normalize-answers.cjs
!.freebuff/patch-stats.cjs
!.freebuff/rotate-stats-answers.cjs
!.freebuff/golden-dump.cjs
!.freebuff/deploy-functions.cjs
!.freebuff/apply-migration.cjs
!.freebuff/apply-mig2.cjs
!.freebuff/get-envkey.cjs
!.freebuff/auto-sync.cjs
# Notes-depth pipeline (docs/notes-depth.md): take the pre-edit snapshot, then
# splice the authored sections in .freebuff/content-depth-appends.cjs into it and
# prove every row clears the gate before anything reaches the live table.
!.freebuff/snapshot-notes-depth.cjs
!.freebuff/build-depth-appends.cjs
# Reusable read-only audit tools, not one-off debug scripts: sql.cjs runs a
# probe file against the live DB, audit-fffd.cjs sweeps every text column for
# the U+FFFD replacement character.
!.freebuff/sql.cjs
!.freebuff/audit-fffd.cjs
# Live verifier for self-service usernames: it asserts the identity rules the
# database owns, with throwaway accounts, and AGENTS.md names it as the check to
# re-run after any change to those rules.
!.freebuff/probe-username-selfservice-live.cjs
# Live verifier for the admin second factor: it measures what an AAL1 session can
# and cannot do, then does the same at AAL2 with a real TOTP code. AGENTS.md names
# it as the check to re-run after touching admin authority or the MFA helpers.
!.freebuff/probe-admin-mfa-live.cjs
# One handle, one account: the underscore-shadow case on the login path and two
# simultaneous claims of the same handle. AGENTS.md names it as the check to
# re-run after touching username resolution or the uniqueness rules.
!.freebuff/probe-username-shadow.cjs
!.freebuff/probe-signup-username-race.cjs
# Phase 3.3's live verifier: spends one Gemini marking call, so it is the only
# proof the English band path runs end to end.
!.freebuff/probe-english-marker-live.cjs
# The before/after matrix that proved deactivating the legacy anon/service_role
# JWTs moved nothing. Re-runnable with no admin credential (signup + SQL).
!.freebuff/probe-legacy-key-cutover.cjs
# The objectives review gate is content pipeline, not a one-off debug script: it
# is the enforcement behind docs/objectives-authoring.md, and AGENTS.md tells an
# author to run it before a topic's objectives are published.
!.freebuff/gate-objectives.cjs
# Route health, not a one-off debug script: drives real Chrome over all 597 study
# routes and is the check AGENTS.md names for "does every page still render",
# plus the throwaway-student maker it signs in with.
!.freebuff/route-health.cjs
!.freebuff/make-verify-student.cjs
# Live verifier for the teacher account type: role + one-subject grant and the
# RLS that keeps the grant read-only from a browser session.
!.freebuff/probe-teacher-live.cjs
# The security regression guard: 24 assertions read from the live catalog (grants,
# definer gates, storage policies, the parent-link RPC). AGENTS.md names it as the
# check to re-run after any migration, and it is what stops anon's write grants
# coming back.
!.freebuff/probe-security-hardening.cjs
# Proves a database backup actually restores: decrypts a real bundle and replays
# its inserts into a scratch schema, comparing every row count to the manifest.
# AGENTS.md names it as the check to re-run after touching the dump/restore code.
!.freebuff/probe-db-restore.cjs
# The notes-depth gate is content pipeline too: it is the enforcement behind
# docs/notes-depth.md, and AGENTS.md tells an author to run it before a deepened
# note is published.
!.freebuff/gate-notes-depth.cjs
# The two notes-depth pipeline steps the docs and AGENTS.md tell an author to
# run: fetch a unit's notes + board statements, then turn a content module into
# guarded SQL. Without them a fresh clone cannot follow docs/notes-depth.md.
!.freebuff/deepen-fetch.cjs
!.freebuff/deepen-materials.cjs
# The edge-function deploy path: ships every .ts file in the function dir so
# relative imports (ai-correction's ./marks.ts) bundle. Without this a fresh
# clone deploys an ai-correction that cannot resolve its own imports.
!.freebuff/redeploy-manage-accounts.cjs
!.freebuff/content-backup/
!.freebuff/pdftool/
# Generated PDF artifacts (booklets, per-topic notes/questions) live in Supabase
# storage; they are rebuildable via pdftool scripts and too large for git.
.freebuff/pdftool/out/
Notes.zip
.temp/

# Local content backups (scripts/backup-content.cjs) — large, machine-specific.
backups/

# Autobuild bundle (rebuildable: scripts/build-single-file.cjs from vite.config.ts).
# Large, machine-specific, and redundant with the project's own build toolchain.
# This project ships via `npm run build` and the Vercel/Render hooks above, so the
# standalone bundle is deliberately excluded from git (and from the deploy manifest
# unless that hook explicitly opts into it).
dist-single/

# One-off spec/extract PDFs and recall-question exports used during content work.
.freebuff-tmp/spec/
.freebuff-tmp/retired-recall-questions.json

# Playtest / QA snapshots generated under this worktree. Not part of the shipped product.

# Playtest / QA snapshots generated under this worktree. Not part of the shipped product.
/freebuff-sites-build/

# Agent scratch directory. A snapshot commit swept this into the public repo
# and carried a live Supabase access token with it (2026-10-14 → 2026-10-29).
# Whole directory, not a file list: the scratch set changes every session.
.freebuff-tmp/
